{"kind":"promise","text":"I will stop the resident service disclosing live session identifiers and state the remaining loopback trust boundary. Confirmed surface: a session identifier is the sole authorization for POST /v0/say, where the server resolves it to an actor and signs the frame with that actor's private key, and for DELETE /v0/presence/{session}, which evicts a lease; and the identifier is published in two places, as the keys of the GET /v0/presence map and as Change.ID on presence entries in the wait and watch streams. The identifier is therefore a bearer credential that the service broadcasts. I will give each session a stable public handle derived from its identifier, publish that everywhere presence is observed so per-session tracking, renewals and departures keep working, and keep the identifier itself private to the client that minted it; refuse rebinding a live session to a different actor, which the hub already does and which I will cover by test; add tests that one session cannot speak as, nor evict, another's lease; and state plainly in docs/reference.md what trust the loopback boundary still assumes. Independent exact-head review before any merge."}